DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(cos(x))^2+4*(sqrt(x))+1");
$fun_1 = Formula("(4/(x))^2+4*(x*3)+1");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("({6, 10} U {8, 10}) U {6, 10} U {-5, -3, -2, 2, 8}");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{8, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {6, 10}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {8, 10})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("([5, infinity) - (6, infinity))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[5, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [5, infinity)) U ([5, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`13/5.32+14*14.32`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('202.923609023'),width=>6}
---

What is the value of [`15.7+16.68+11.97+15`]? [_____]{answer=>59.35,width=>10}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 5\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cap A \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{8, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, -3, -2, 2, 8\}`]
- [`C = \{6, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C \cup A) \cup C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cap C \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, -10, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, -6, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, -6, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, -10, -9>") x Compute("<-5, -6, -2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -10, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, -10, -9>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, -10, -9>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, 10, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 9, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, 9, -1>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 9, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 10, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 10, -3>") . Compute("<2, 9, -1>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 9, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 10, -3>") x Compute("<2, 9, -1>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>0)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
